    "datasource": "Fujichrome T64 Professional [RTP], Fujifilm AF3-178E; SHA256 5cd6002052da6e87600b3cfc2e1f4b3bc6d97bf526e4654cf7befc6db34e0dc0. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/fuji-t64/recipe.json. Dye spectra: this sheet, with no plotted neutral to rescale against. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Not on the sheet. The dye panel is normalised to a visual neutral of 1.0 and plots no D-min, and the characteristic panel's minimum is a status-A reading, not a spectral curve. A flat 0.10 is assumed, within the 0.09-0.13 range the shipped positives carry. This is an assumption, not a measurement. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from fujifilm_provia_100f. Nearest shipped sibling: the same manufacturer's E-6 reversal family. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.8852, 1.0587, 1.0192], log-exposure shift [0.0319, 0.0, 0.0546], data_trustability 0.2. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 56.1% before, 1.3% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
